@* KpiTile.razor — Phase 8 (REQ-UI-01..04). Click delegates to OnSelected; the parent
   KpiTileBar composes the bidirectional sync with FilterChipGroup Status chip. The
   IsActive flag drives the 3px --bs-primary left-border and the elevated shadow;
   non-active tiles use the default flat AdminLTE card.

   Markup contract LOCKED in 08-UI-SPEC.md §Components/Shared/KpiTile.razor.
   Pixel anatomy LOCKED in 08-UI-SPEC.md §KpiTile pixel anatomy:
     - 100% width of parent grid column (col-md-3 / col-sm-6 / col-12 — KpiTileBar wraps)
     - intrinsic ~96px height (16px padding + 40px count + 4px gap + 14px label + 16px padding)
     - 3px --bs-primary left-border + elevated shadow when IsActive
     - hover lifts to --bs-tertiary-bg (light) / [data-bs-theme="dark"] variant in scoped CSS

   Native <button type="button"> for keyboard/ARIA correctness — Enter / Space activate
   via natural <button> semantics; aria-pressed reflects IsActive (REQ-UI-01). The 40px
   count font-size lives in the scoped .razor.css (NOT inline) per 08-UI-SPEC §Permitted
   Inline Style Exceptions: the typography exception is bounded to the .kpi-count selector. *@

<button type="button"
        class="card kpi-tile w-100 text-start p-0 border-0 @(IsActive ? "kpi-tile-active" : "") @BackgroundClass"
        aria-pressed="@IsActive.ToString().ToLowerInvariant()"
        @onclick="OnSelectedAsync">
    <div class="card-body p-3">
        <div class="d-flex align-items-center gap-2">
            <i class="bi @IconClass" style="font-size: 1.25rem;" aria-hidden="true"></i>
            <span class="kpi-count fw-semibold">@Count</span>
        </div>
        <small class="text-body-secondary mt-1 d-block">@Label</small>
    </div>
</button>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Label { get; set; } = "";
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public int Count { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string IconClass { get; set; } = "bi-collection-fill";
    [Parameter] public bool IsActive { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnSelected { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string BackgroundClass { get; set; } = "";

    private Task OnSelectedAsync() => OnSelected.InvokeAsync();
}
